  "term": "homovanillic acid",
  "definition": "Homovanillic acid is a monocarboxylic acid produced when catecholamines are broken down. It can be measured as a biological marker of metabolic stress, tobacco use, or catecholamine-secreting tumors such as neuroblastoma or pheochromocytoma.",
